{{USTV|1996}}
These are the late night schedules for the four United States broadcast networks that offer programming during this time period, from September 1996 to August 1997. All times are Eastern or Pacific. Affiliates will fill non-network schedule with local, syndicated, or paid programming. Affiliates also have the option to preempt or delay network programming at their discretion.

In February 1997, [[Jay Leno]] took [[NBC]]'s ''[[The Tonight Show with Jay Leno|The Tonight Show]]'' on the road for a week, hosting his late-night television show at the [[MGM Grand Las Vegas]].<ref name=":0">{{Cite news |date=February 3, 1997 |title=Leno's 'Tonight Show' spends week on road |url=https://www.newspapers.com/article/the-springfield-news-leader-lenos-toni/204352664/ |access-date=2026-08-22 |work=The Springfield News-Leader |via=[[Newspapers.com]]}}</ref> Meanwhile on [[CBS]], [[David Letterman]] held a month-long celebration on ''[[Late Show with David Letterman|The Late Show]]'' celebrating his 15 years in [[Late-night television in the United States|American late-night television]].<ref name=":0" />

